[{:db/id "q-9749/selection/6e3b4e7a0b20e6f5f8e88a5bf12cbb2100ba7ca4807ef4184b19cce5d851665d" :answer/id #uuid "e1338150-8dee-5635-b2b7-90b6e36e1bfe" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{6}(1-{4}^{N})" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-9749/selection/451fad2a41b3c8ad9a88235faa4974cf4f90e16a2a1a335db20ea3e5bf2e4b0c" :answer/id #uuid "8581926b-a68e-50bd-bb10-4e76f852d381" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{(\\frac{4}{6})}^{N}-\\frac{1}{6}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-9749/selection/c97bc5a2a19cd5a2ee6642073764a9bc2567ecfe361d302242ccc70a39490ebd" :answer/id #uuid "d88b3f06-dc91-56da-972c-ee6f11e78f2e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{6}({4}^{N}-1)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-9749/selection/292e9a8d71f900e5e64d8cea1c4a97eb267493b6e9699cb840f07aca9d2d829b" :answer/id #uuid "7de65e78-fe90-5a32-9cb1-0301bdc86afc" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{(\\frac{4}{6})}^{N}+\\frac{1}{6}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-9749/selection/e487873bc728c7fe0b9bd817a2ab52f98f5023ae6dc3a070266c39b3ea242c93" :answer/id #uuid "4d59f86f-91a9-5d13-9756-4acbc5a06541" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{6}({4}^{N}+1)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-9749/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "0bd95049-5642-5a48-968c-70603aa94243" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-9749/selection/c97bc5a2a19cd5a2ee6642073764a9bc2567ecfe361d302242ccc70a39490ebd" :answer-field/choices ["q-9749/selection/6e3b4e7a0b20e6f5f8e88a5bf12cbb2100ba7ca4807ef4184b19cce5d851665d" "q-9749/selection/451fad2a41b3c8ad9a88235faa4974cf4f90e16a2a1a335db20ea3e5bf2e4b0c" "q-9749/selection/c97bc5a2a19cd5a2ee6642073764a9bc2567ecfe361d302242ccc70a39490ebd" "q-9749/selection/292e9a8d71f900e5e64d8cea1c4a97eb267493b6e9699cb840f07aca9d2d829b" "q-9749/selection/e487873bc728c7fe0b9bd817a2ab52f98f5023ae6dc3a070266c39b3ea242c93"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-9749" :question/id #uuid "78fba3be-7310-5e50-9e3c-f6710527699a" :question/math-academy-id "q-9749" :question/problem "What is the sum of the first $N$ terms of a series $\\frac{1}{2}+2+8+⋯?$" :question/worked-solution "Note that $\\frac{1}{2}+2+8+⋯$ is the sum of a geometric series since the ratio of any two consecutive terms is constant.\n\nFirst, we determine the common ratio $r$ for this geometric series:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =\\frac{{a}_{2}}{{a}_{1}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{(\\frac{1}{2})} \\\\  & =4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe sum of the first $N$ terms of a geometric series can be determined by the formula\n\n$$\n{S}_{N}=\\frac{{a}_{1}(1-{r}^{N})}{1-r}.\n$$\n\nIn this case ${a}_{1}=\\frac{1}{2}$ and $r=4.$ Substituting these values into the formula for ${S}_{N}$ gives the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{S}_{N} & =\\frac{{a}_{1}(1-{r}^{N})}{1-r} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\frac{1}{2}(1-{4}^{N})}{1-4} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\frac{1}{2}(1-{4}^{N})}{-3} \\\\  & =\\frac{(\\frac{1}{2})}{3}\\cdot ({4}^{N}-1) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{6}({4}^{N}-1)\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-9749/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "c17552f7-0720-5e45-9c79-7db73e332045"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-9749"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-39996/selection/603f7cfb79055bd8200e3ae38666523994700fa410708740da237f4b96af4b47" :answer/id #uuid "4f21bd8b-579f-572e-827a-1f5096bffa1a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{3}{4}({5}^{N}-1)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-39996/selection/ce83974e25f22184faf643eea79ae2a4eb53bf5c1ffc94c601e7d6b297dbbb6d" :answer/id #uuid "1f1a2642-e2b7-5b7d-abbe-5ebb9e7f8598" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}({5}^{N}-1)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-39996/selection/7a44d01f245444b8f2e2e9d3f0c2ac88d44f9bec8f771d81659d0efd48c59fc5" :answer/id #uuid "a669d986-b3bd-5d5d-abae-1611c020cf6f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{3}{4}(1-{5}^{N})" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-39996/selection/a0ae597c5f02b5073afa762500f9f6e83f4f0b47e52e05a40f171d74176737e1" :answer/id #uuid "4073891e-8a98-5727-9414-3b1801fbe3dc" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{5}{3}({3}^{N}-1)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-39996/selection/a7e1c9f6530881e55e7bc523ef7476a95aaa5bdf4fd99a68c1c9c70a1005e9ce" :answer/id #uuid "e81f080b-0b8c-5f3f-88dd-050066b91727" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{5}{3}(1-{3}^{N})" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-39996/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "bd5b44dc-ca0f-5f74-81cc-6b5116cc8922" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-39996/selection/603f7cfb79055bd8200e3ae38666523994700fa410708740da237f4b96af4b47" :answer-field/choices ["q-39996/selection/603f7cfb79055bd8200e3ae38666523994700fa410708740da237f4b96af4b47" "q-39996/selection/ce83974e25f22184faf643eea79ae2a4eb53bf5c1ffc94c601e7d6b297dbbb6d" "q-39996/selection/7a44d01f245444b8f2e2e9d3f0c2ac88d44f9bec8f771d81659d0efd48c59fc5" "q-39996/selection/a0ae597c5f02b5073afa762500f9f6e83f4f0b47e52e05a40f171d74176737e1" "q-39996/selection/a7e1c9f6530881e55e7bc523ef7476a95aaa5bdf4fd99a68c1c9c70a1005e9ce"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-39996" :question/id #uuid "968d763f-7575-5b03-8e25-e8e3c2bafb23" :question/math-academy-id "q-39996" :question/problem "What is the sum of the first $N$ terms of a geometric series $3+15+75+⋯\\,?$" :question/worked-solution "First, we determine the common ratio $r$ for this geometric series:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =\\frac{{a}_{2}}{{a}_{1}} \\\\  & =\\frac{15}{3} \\\\  & =5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe sum of the first $N$ terms of a geometric series can be determined by the formula\n\n$$\n{S}_{N}=\\frac{{a}_{1}(1-{r}^{N})}{1-r}.\n$$\n\nIn this case ${a}_{1}=3$ and $r=5.$ Substituting these values into the formula for ${S}_{N}$ gives the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{S}_{N} & =\\frac{{a}_{1}(1-{r}^{N})}{1-r} \\\\  & =\\frac{3(1-{5}^{N})}{1-5} \\\\  & =\\frac{3(1-{5}^{N})}{(-4)} \\\\  & =-\\frac{3}{4}(1-{5}^{N}) \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{4}({5}^{N}-1)\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-39996/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "c17552f7-0720-5e45-9c79-7db73e332045"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-39996"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-67104/selection/c108d925a3be2abf3e4317777ee6b153c254ba65af0437bf4056e56ea9b23cc0" :answer/id #uuid "fd9fe08c-7ac4-5c96-8a4a-2c0643379b7e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{3}^{N}-1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-67104/selection/5ac2a59f7073a66078ed46dacd61461212e4869184355c765a368563fd0de5c9" :answer/id #uuid "1ee4b3bb-2e41-5c34-8d7a-5d57d77bf837" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{4}^{N}-12" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-67104/selection/a2f98f82476eecef367665140b798c63415d33e9502991c196d9101dfa44d165" :answer/id #uuid "3955e9ec-c0be-5304-aa2f-c1504cba7382" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4({3}^{N}-1)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-67104/selection/5293563bb36bbe32e37d6ef478676e9fa175bf61d3e411246fc6b71a462b3452" :answer/id #uuid "c856e8d0-7aa7-5451-8e1d-432d7978f28a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{4}^{N}-1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-67104/selection/b795818cc28779bcbe410a46f186c45d5c86bfa3132bca88ed831dbfc7217405" :answer/id #uuid "a87447b3-4978-57b6-88e3-a3b4fc692a91" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3({4}^{N}-1)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-67104/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "9124a7fe-87cf-5f88-be2b-e8c915c23b03" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-67104/selection/5293563bb36bbe32e37d6ef478676e9fa175bf61d3e411246fc6b71a462b3452" :answer-field/choices ["q-67104/selection/c108d925a3be2abf3e4317777ee6b153c254ba65af0437bf4056e56ea9b23cc0" "q-67104/selection/5ac2a59f7073a66078ed46dacd61461212e4869184355c765a368563fd0de5c9" "q-67104/selection/a2f98f82476eecef367665140b798c63415d33e9502991c196d9101dfa44d165" "q-67104/selection/5293563bb36bbe32e37d6ef478676e9fa175bf61d3e411246fc6b71a462b3452" "q-67104/selection/b795818cc28779bcbe410a46f186c45d5c86bfa3132bca88ed831dbfc7217405"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-67104" :question/id #uuid "595b4600-8002-5fc9-aae5-7663d61dcae3" :question/math-academy-id "q-67104" :question/problem "What is the sum of the first $N$ terms of a geometric series if the $4$th term is $192$ and the common ratio is $4?$" :question/worked-solution "We use the formula for the $n$th term of a geometric sequence to determine ${a}_{1}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{n} & ={a}_{1}{r}^{n-1} \\\\ 192 & ={a}_{1}\\cdot {4}^{(4-1)} \\\\ 192 & =64{a}_{1} \\\\ {a}_{1} & =3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe sum of the first $N$ terms of a geometric series can be determined by the formula\n\n$$\n{S}_{N}=\\frac{{a}_{1}(1-{r}^{N})}{1-r}.\n$$\n\nIn this case, ${a}_{1}=3$ and $r=4.$ Substituting our values into the formula for ${S}_{N}$ gives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{S}_{N} & =\\frac{3(1-{4}^{N})}{1-4} \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{(-3)}(1-{4}^{N}) \\\\  & =-(1-{4}^{N}) \\\\  & ={4}^{N}-1\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-67104/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "bd32a853-e0ec-5d56-bd6b-1c2e0e3249f8"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-67104"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-73425/selection/5293563bb36bbe32e37d6ef478676e9fa175bf61d3e411246fc6b71a462b3452" :answer/id #uuid "ea7adb18-dbfe-5840-975c-125e7a68beeb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{4}^{N}-1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-73425/selection/b795818cc28779bcbe410a46f186c45d5c86bfa3132bca88ed831dbfc7217405" :answer/id #uuid "2c5301bb-0b79-5e78-8fd1-fddf6a2df8db" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3({4}^{N}-1)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-73425/selection/44d16fee5f2f01f8c8fcbc3c6686c2a462a238f810495cfb2107930832f2fa95" :answer/id #uuid "2389d4a2-b843-5528-9175-9f2fd09ff939" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2({4}^{N}-1)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-73425/selection/e7f22b5b2265521db19cf489cbee1e9640036466c8cad64354468edd7138bd0f" :answer/id #uuid "b999a01c-f4e0-5c76-83d4-2036f54dc55b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{4}^{N}-3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-73425/selection/66d8604e1bed4e9d41141bf0a5241086e4060630c837ef68742eb52c5071f861" :answer/id #uuid "25f2836d-01f8-5701-bb63-b68b0ebfdda2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{4}^{N}-2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-73425/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "92b18c56-2e57-5839-acc8-ce5670f616a7" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-73425/selection/44d16fee5f2f01f8c8fcbc3c6686c2a462a238f810495cfb2107930832f2fa95" :answer-field/choices ["q-73425/selection/5293563bb36bbe32e37d6ef478676e9fa175bf61d3e411246fc6b71a462b3452" "q-73425/selection/b795818cc28779bcbe410a46f186c45d5c86bfa3132bca88ed831dbfc7217405" "q-73425/selection/44d16fee5f2f01f8c8fcbc3c6686c2a462a238f810495cfb2107930832f2fa95" "q-73425/selection/e7f22b5b2265521db19cf489cbee1e9640036466c8cad64354468edd7138bd0f" "q-73425/selection/66d8604e1bed4e9d41141bf0a5241086e4060630c837ef68742eb52c5071f861"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-73425" :question/id #uuid "9360a987-6868-5ee3-a005-1b57385aa970" :question/math-academy-id "q-73425" :question/problem "What is the sum of the first $N$ terms of a geometric series if the $4$th term is $384$ and the common ratio is $4?$" :question/worked-solution "We use the formula for the $n$th term of a geometric sequence to determine ${a}_{1}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{n} & ={a}_{1}{r}^{n-1} \\\\ 384 & ={a}_{1}\\cdot {4}^{(4-1)} \\\\ 384 & ={a}_{1}\\cdot {4}^{3} \\\\ 384 & =64{a}_{1} \\\\ {a}_{1} & =6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe sum of the first $N$ terms of a geometric series can be determined by the formula\n\n$$\n{S}_{N}=\\frac{{a}_{1}(1-{r}^{N})}{1-r}.\n$$\n\nIn this case, ${a}_{1}=6$ and $r=4.$ Substituting our values into the formula for ${S}_{N}$ gives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{S}_{N} & =\\frac{6(1-{4}^{N})}{1-4} \\\\  & =\\frac{6}{(-3)}(1-{4}^{N}) \\\\  & =-2(1-{4}^{N}) \\\\  & =2({4}^{N}-1)\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-73425/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "bd32a853-e0ec-5d56-bd6b-1c2e0e3249f8"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-73425"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-276486/field-1/9c3ecdcec06f99fc2ad50225b6d261980fd2e2fcfafa50f24a31c583639a4f00" :answer/id #uuid "fbb9e2ef-e6f4-5842-a54f-22a5a581cf07" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{5}{3}(4^N-1)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-276486/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "6171aebd-b144-5756-9dde-eb8785171ba3" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-276486/field-1/9c3ecdcec06f99fc2ad50225b6d261980fd2e2fcfafa50f24a31c583639a4f00" :answer-field/choices ["q-276486/field-1/9c3ecdcec06f99fc2ad50225b6d261980fd2e2fcfafa50f24a31c583639a4f00"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-276486" :question/id #uuid "a5731125-307e-51c6-9f9a-f16cf62d6761" :question/math-academy-id "q-276486" :question/problem "What is the sum of the first $N$ terms of a geometric series if the $4$th term is $320$ and the common ratio is $4?$ Express your answer as a function of $N,$ making sure you use a capital letter $(N,$ not $n).$\n\n${S}_{N}=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "We use the formula for the $n$th term of a geometric sequence to determine ${a}_{1}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{n} & ={a}_{1}{r}^{n-1} \\\\ 320 & ={a}_{1}\\cdot {4}^{(4-1)} \\\\ 320 & =64{a}_{1} \\\\ {a}_{1} & =5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe sum of the first $N$ terms of a geometric series can be determined by the formula\n\n$$\n{S}_{N}=\\frac{{a}_{1}(1-{r}^{N})}{1-r}.\n$$\n\nIn this case, ${a}_{1}=5$ and $r=4.$ Substituting our values into the formula for ${S}_{N}$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{S}_{N} & =\\frac{5(1-{4}^{N})}{1-4} \\\\  & =\\frac{5(1-{4}^{N})}{(-3)} \\\\  & =-\\frac{5}{3}(1-{4}^{N}) \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{3}({4}^{N}-1).\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-276486/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "bd32a853-e0ec-5d56-bd6b-1c2e0e3249f8"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-276486"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]}]
